# Corpus licence

The eight documents in `rfc/` are verbatim RFC text published by the RFC Editor on behalf
of the IETF Trust.

**Terms.** RFC documents are made available under the IETF Trust Legal Provisions (TLP),
which permit reproduction and distribution of IETF Documents. Each document carries its own
copyright notice, and those notices are preserved in `rfc/` — the cleaner keeps everything
from the Abstract onwards, which includes the "Copyright Notice" section of every file.

- Trust Legal Provisions: https://trustee.ietf.org/license-info/
- The grant from contributors to the Trust is described in RFC 5378, section 5.3:
  https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5378

**What was changed.** Only page furniture: running page headers, page footers, form feeds,
the IETF front matter block, and the table of contents. The body text, section numbering,
reference lists and author addresses are unmodified. The exact transformation is
`scripts/fetch_corpus.py`, and `corpus/SOURCES.json` records a SHA-256 of both the downloaded
original and the cleaned file, so anyone can verify the claim rather than trust it.

**What is not claimed.** This project is not affiliated with the IETF. Nothing here is an
IETF publication, and a citation produced by `scout` is a citation to the RFC, not an
endorsement by its authors.
